ISO-10303-21;
/* Wr016: Re-output of intermediate construction entities (orphan geometry); DATA section contains CARTESIAN_POINT, LINE, and CIRCLE entities not referenced by any PRODUCT_DEFINITION_SHAPE chain; construction-history scratch geometry is not pruned before export; model is correct but file is bloated 3-5x by orphan geometry; common in Pro/E exports of complex parts with sketch history; writers that emit every kernel-internal entity including scratch geometry; expected kernel behavior: parse normally; ignore unreferenced entities; a re-emit pass may normalize/prune; a strict policy emits a warning; synonyms: STEP file has unreferenced entities, orphan geometry in DATA section, construction history not pruned, STEP file unnecessarily large */
